b = \\Delta + ib\\left(\\frac d2 + x\\cdot\\nabla\\right)$ in homogeneous Sobolev spaces and energy space $H^1$. The deformed Laplacian $\\Delta_b$ arises from the renormalization and its operator group $e^{it\\Delta_b}$ exhibits self-similar dispersion, which not only recovers the free Strichartz but also enables an extension of resolvent families. Compared with Strichartz estimates based on $\\Delta$, this one has a larger admissible region, works for arbitrarily small polynomial decaying potential, and requires no spectral assumption.\n\nHow the literature uses it\n\n### 5 arXiv papers cite this in 16 sentences\n\nEach citing sentence is taken from the citing paper's LaTeX source and typed by Pith's classifier. A label appears at probability 0.8 or more, a contest at 0.7 or more; the quoted words are the citing authors'. How each label was checked · JSON\n\nPapers citing it · 9 sentences without a confident label\n\nUses its method or tool 2 papers\n\n  * > From the boundedness of $R_b^+$ in [ref] and density argument, it suffices to estimate for Schwartz functions $f ∈𝒮(^d)$, and the Fourier representation in [ref] (R_b^+(z)f)(rω) = i/br^-d/2 + z/b e^ir^2/2b-iz/b lnr ∫_r^∞ρ^d/2 - 1 - z/b e^-iρ^2/2b+iz/b lnρ f̂(ρω) dρ. is valid.\n\nMode stability for self-similar blowup of slightly supercritical NLS: II. high-energy spectrum · A priori estimates for eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of $_b$ · 0.82\n\n  * > This matching initial data argument comes from [ref] .\n\nNonradial stability of self-similar blowup to Keller-Segel equation in three dimensions · Sketch of proof. · 1.00\n\nCites it as support 1 paper\n\n  * > Based on [ref] , the missing piece towards asymptotic stability of $Q_b$ is a sharp spectral analysis to count exactly the unstable directions, or rather, to derive mode stability of this linearized operator.\n\nMode stability for self-similar blowup of slightly supercritical NLS: I. low-energy spectrum · Setting and background · 0.87\n\nCites it as backgr